AB  - This study explores how modern horticulture can benefit from the integration of Web of Things (IoT) advancements to tackle issues such as soil health, water management, and yield efficiency. Researches can use screen fundamental parameters like soil moisture, temperature, and mugginess using IoT-powered sensors, drones, and artificial intelligence, enabling information- driven guidance. The review examines current IoT systems and structures for astute farming, highlighting their potential to increase horticultural efficiency, cut down on waste, and meet the growing demand for sustenance projected for 2050. Mechanized water systems, bug-the-executives, and continuous harvest yield expectations are some of the key applications. In any event, challenges are present, such as high execution costs and limited openness for ranchers with limited scope. The analysis emphasizes the need for sensible IoT arrangements, specific planning, and methodical approaches.  © 2025 IEEE.
