AU  - Rahmani, M.; Asgari, J.; Asgarimehr, M.
TI  - Soil moisture retrieval using space-borne GNSS reflectometry: a comprehensive review
T2  - International Journal of Remote Sensing
LA  - English
KW  - Bi-static radar; CYGNSS; GNSS-R; soil moisture; TDS-1; Agriculture; Moisture control; Remote sensing; Satellites; Soil surveys; Space optics; Space-based radar; Agricultural irrigation; Bistatic radars; CYGNSS; GNSS-R; Irrigation management; Reflectometry; Soil moisture monitoring; Soil moisture retrievals; Space-borne; TDS-1; GNSS; radar; reflectometry; remote sensing; soil moisture; Soil moisture
AB  - Accurate knowledge of soil moisture is critical for hydrological and agricultural applications such as agricultural irrigation management, drought characterization, and flood detection. Researchers have attempted to provide soil moisture using various methods and techniques. Traditionally, the amount of soil moisture was based on field measurements. On the other hand, remote sensing satellites have been widely used to provide continuous soil moisture measurements worldwide, encountering problems such as the lack of simultaneous spatial and temporal sampling rates and dependence on weather conditions. However, in recent decades, GNSS signals reflected from the Earth’s surface (GNSS-R technique) have been increasingly used for soil moisture monitoring, due to the numerous advantages it offers. This paper aims to provide a comprehensive review of soil moisture retrieved by two space-based GNSS-R missions (TDS-1 and CYGNSS) to show the general past trends, gaps, and opportunities for soil moisture monitoring through GNSS-R observations. © 2022 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
